  #line-at(72.1pt, 84.08pt, "interfacial activation compromise long-term transport stability over a 25-year operating ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 105.1pt, "horizon. ")
  #line-at(90.125pt, 131.37pt, "Simultaneously, economic and supply pressures are driving the industry to explore ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 152.37pt, "alternatives to silver metallization [7,20]. Screen printed TOPCon cells typically consume ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 172.65pt, "between 9 and 15 mg/W  of silver, and roadmaps target reductions below 2 mg/W through ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 193.67pt, "hybrid Ag Cu pastes or full copper electroplating [20]. Copper metallized silicon ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 214.7pt, "heterojunction devices have demonstrated efficiencies within approximately 0.4 percent ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 234.95pt, "absolute of silver references, confirming technical feasibility at the cell level [21–23]. ")
  #line-at(90.125pt, 261.97pt, "Copper introduces distinct interfacial chemistry, including different diffusion kinetics, ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 282.25pt, "oxidation susceptibility, and potential contamination pathways [6,22]. These differences may ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 303.28pt, "alter the balance between contact resistivity and recombination relative to silver systems [24]. ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 324.28pt, "A critical open question is whether copper-based contacts avoid the transport stability ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 344.55pt, "tradeoffs observed in LECO activated silver systems or whether similar hydrogen related or ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 365.58pt, "diffusion driven instabilities emerge under long term operation [6]. The material transition ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 385.85pt, "may therefore redistribute rather than eliminate the interfacial constraint. ")
  #line-at(90.125pt, 412.85pt, "As silicon architectures approach practical efficiency ceilings near 28 percent, ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 433.87pt, "incremental performance gains increasingly depend on resolving interfacial transport and ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 454.15pt, "long term stability constraints rather than bulk absorber limitations [21,25]. Metallization has ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 475.17pt, "therefore emerged as a system level determinant of both manufacturing viability and field ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 495.42pt, "durability. The framework presented here provides a basis for evaluating silver and copper ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 516.45pt, "contact strategies under a common set of physical principles, with the goal of enabling high ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 537.47pt, "initial efficiency without compromising 25-year reliability. ")
  #line-at(90.125pt, 563.75pt, "This review develops a unified electrical and mechanistic framework to analyze these ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 584.77pt, "coupled effects. Instead of treating contact resistance, recombination, material selection, and ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 605.02pt, "reliability as isolated metrics, total series resistance is decomposed into contributions from ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 626.05pt, "emitter sheet resistance, contact geometry and transfer width, and interfacial barrier ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 646.33pt, "properties. Recombination losses are evaluated through ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(341.68pt, 646.33pt, "𝑗")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 8.25pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(345.45pt, 649.33pt, "0,met")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(367.22pt, 646.33pt, " and their impact on implied ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(506.15pt, 646.33pt, "𝑉")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 8.25pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(511.4pt, 649.33pt, "oc")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(519.65pt, 646.33pt, ". ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 668.83pt, "By integrating transport, recombination, and stability within a single analytical structure, the ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 689.85pt, "review clarifies the reliability to trade space governing next generation metallization. ")
]

