// arXiv source page 24
#original-page(595.5pt, 841.5pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(458.07pt, 792.7pt, "Page 24 of 51 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.75pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.1pt, 803.95pt, "Donald Intal & Abasifreke U. Ebong: ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.75pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(226.05pt, 803.95pt, "Preprint submitted to Elsevier")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90.125pt, 84.08pt, "Copper is a fast diffuser in crystalline silicon, with transport pathways that include grain ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 105.1pt, "boundaries, defective dielectrics, and precipitate networks [113]. If Cu reaches electrically ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 125.35pt, "active regions of the device, it can form Cu-rich clusters and Cu")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.25pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(379.98pt, 126.1pt, "3")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(384.5pt, 125.35pt, "Si, which introduce strong ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 146.37pt, "recombination activity and can reduce minority carrier diffusion length [6,114]. For this ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 166.65pt, "reason, Cu metallization schemes rely on barrier concepts that both suppress Cu transport and ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 187.67pt, "provide a controlled interfacial reaction layer for low resistance contact formation [115]. ")
  #line-at(90.125pt, 214.7pt, "From a reliability perspective, the critical issue is whether the interfacial reaction remains ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 234.95pt, "thin, continuous, and mechanically intact, or whether it transitions into uncontrolled ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 255.97pt, "penetration as defined by the microstructural classification in Section 3.2. In the controlled ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 276.25pt, "regime, a bounded silicide layer improves adhesion and contact resistivity while blocking ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 297.25pt, "further Cu motion [114]. In the uncontrolled regime, excessive thermal budget or local barrier ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 318.28pt, "imperfections allow Cu to bypass the intended diffusion block, promoting thicker, irregular ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 338.55pt, "silicide growth, voiding driven by unequal atomic fluxes, and local cracking [115,116]. Once ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 359.58pt, "cracks or void networks form, they act as fast paths that couple Cu transport to electrically ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 379.83pt, "sensitive regions, increasing the probability of deep shunting and junction degradation over ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 400.85pt, "time [6]. In LECO assisted Cu concepts, the process window must therefore be defined not ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 421.12pt, "only by achieving low ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(182.47pt, 421.12pt, "ρ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 8.25pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(189.25pt, 424.12pt, "𝑐")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(193.75pt, 421.12pt, ", but also by keeping silicide thickness, morphology, and barrier ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 442.9pt, "integrity within a bounded design space. ")
  #line-at(90.125pt, 469.15pt, "A second coupling is packaging chemistry. Moisture and encapsulant degradation ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 490.18pt, "products can facilitate Cu transport or complexation, effectively lowering the barrier for Cu ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 510.45pt, "migration under damp heat and bias [6]. As a result, the same interfacial stack can appear ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 531.47pt, "stable or unstable depending on the module environment. For Cu systems, long term stability ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 552.48pt, "is therefore a system property of the contact stack plus encapsulation, rather than a ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 572.75pt, "metallization only attribute, an interaction that is captured at the architecture level in Table 4. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 15.775pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.1pt, 605.02pt, "6.2 Electromigration under current crowding ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90.125pt, 633.55pt, "Even when diffusion is well controlled by barrier design, LECO activated contacts can ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 653.83pt, "remain vulnerable to current density driven transport because current flow at the interface is ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 674.85pt, "typically not uniform. As developed in Sections 3.3 and 4.2, conduction can be dominated by ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 695.1pt, "a sparse network of high conductance microcontacts and filaments, which increases local ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 716.13pt, "current density and concentrates Joule heating at a small subset of sites. Such current ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 737.15pt, "localization activates electromigration, especially in fine line metallization where the line ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 757.425pt, "cross section is reduced and module operating temperatures can be elevated [6,107]. ")
]

// arXiv source page 25
#original-page(595.5pt, 841.5pt, (image("graphics/page-25.png", width: 335.5pt), 131pt, 379.5pt))[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(458.07pt, 792.7pt, "Page 25 of 51 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.75pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.1pt, 803.95pt, "Donald Intal & Abasifreke U. Ebong: ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.75pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(226.05pt, 803.95pt, "Preprint submitted to Elsevier")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90.125pt, 84.08pt, "Electromigration risk is amplified by two reinforcing factors. First, current crowding, ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 105.1pt, "which raises the local J and therefore the driving force for atomic flux, while also increasing ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 124.6pt, "local J")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.25pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(102.87pt, 120.85pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(110.4pt, 124.6pt, "ρ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(117.15pt, 124.6pt, " heating, which accelerates mass transport through temperature dependent ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 146.37pt, "diffusivities [107]. Second, thermal cycling, which  introduces cyclic mechanical stress at ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 167.4pt, "interfaces between metal, glass, and silicon [117]. These interfaces are often the same regions ")
