  #line-at(72.1pt, 87.08pt, "6.3 Damp heat corrosion ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90.125pt, 115.6pt, "Environmental exposure introduces chemical drivers that can either act independently ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 136.62pt, "(pure contact corrosion) or serve as enablers for other failure modes (barrier degradation that ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 156.9pt, "accelerates diffusion). Damp heat exposure accelerates corrosion reactions involving ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 177.9pt, "metallization, interfacial glass layers, and encapsulant degradation products [117]. For Ag-")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 198.92pt, "based fired contacts, a common pathway is chemical modification of the glass phase at the ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 219.2pt, "metal glass silicon interface. Organic acids and ionic species generated during encapsulant ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 240.2pt, "aging can leach modifiers from the glass network, weaken adhesion, and create porosity and ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 260.47pt, "voids at the triple line region [107,121]. These microstructural changes increase contact ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 281.5pt, "resistance and can also promote localized delamination, which further concentrates current ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 302.53pt, "and accelerates resistive heating. ")
  #line-at(90.125pt, 328.8pt, "Cu-based systems share the same general vulnerability to moisture assisted corrosion but ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 349.8pt, "add a diffusion driven failure channel: once corrosion or cracking compromises a barrier, Cu ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 370.08pt, "transport into silicon can accelerate, potentially leading to junction leakage and shunt ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 391.1pt, "formation [6,115]. In this sense, corrosion and diffusion are coupled rather than independent; ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 411.35pt, "corrosion can be the initiator that turns an otherwise stable diffusion barrier into an active ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 432.37pt, "diffusion conduit. ")
  #line-at(90.125pt, 459.4pt, "LECO can modify the corrosion landscape in either direction depending on how it ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 479.67pt, "restructures the interface. If LECO reduces aggressive glass spikes and improves electrical ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 500.7pt, "coupling through a more stable microcontact ensemble, it may lower local overpotentials and ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 520.95pt, "reduce the tendency for corrosion driven resistance drift. Conversely, localized thermal and ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 541.97pt, "mechanical gradients can introduce microcracks or expose fresh metal silicon protrusions that ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 563pt, "become preferential pathways for moisture and ionic species [107]. The resulting electrical ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 583.25pt, "signatures can therefore differ: corrosion dominated transport loss typically presents as ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 603.53pt, "increasing ")
