  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#0e2841"))
  #line-at(506.15pt, 346.8pt, " for ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 357.33pt, "Stable (optimized), Marginal (near-threshold), and Laten damage. Stable remains tightly clustered, marginal shows ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 367.83pt, "increased scatter, and latent damage exhibits the largest parameter shifts and efficiency loss (data compiled from ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 378.32pt, "[5,15,17,76,108,121–125]). ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90.125pt, 402.35pt, "Processing points that lie well inside Zone II and remain stable during environmental ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 422.62pt, "stress exhibit small and approximately monotonic electrical drift. In this regime, degradation ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 443.65pt, "is dominated by slow metallization aging rather than abrupt interfacial transitions [116,117]. ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 464.65pt, "The fill factor decreases gradually with limited device-to-device scatter, and no systematic ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 484.92pt, "leakage paths emerge. The microcontact network remains statistically uniform, current ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 505.95pt, "localization is moderate, and diffusion processes proceed at rates consistent with ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 526.2pt, "conventional long-term aging rather than instability-driven failure. ")
  #line-at(90.125pt, 553.22pt, "As processing approaches either the Zone I to Zone II activation boundary or the Zone II ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 574.25pt, "to Zone III damaged boundary, the stability margin narrows. Here the microcontact ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 594.53pt, "population may be sparse, or the interface may only marginally exceed the activation ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 615.55pt, "threshold. Small variations in glass distribution, barrier continuity, or silicide morphology ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 635.8pt, "then produce disproportionately large variations in current localization [6,118]. Under stress, ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 656.08pt, "aging accelerates and electrical signatures become mixed: ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(353.7pt, 656.08pt, "𝑅")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 8.25pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(361.2pt, 659.07pt, "s")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(364.97pt, 656.08pt, " may rise due to contact ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 677.85pt, "degradation while localized leakage begins to appear in the weakest regions [122]. The ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 698.85pt, "defining characteristic of this regime is high statistical scatter rather than uniform drift, ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 719.13pt, "reflecting the sensitivity of transport to local microstructural heterogeneity. ")
  #line-at(90.125pt, 746.15pt, "A third trajectory emerges when processing conditions initially place devices within Zone ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 766.425pt, "II based on IV metrics, yet the interfacial state is only metastable under prolonged electrical ")
]

