  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#0e2841"))
  #line-at(282.35pt, 376.83pt, ", and calibrated surrogate models convert the metrics into process ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 387.35pt, "windows and digital-twin control linking recipe settings to interface state and reliability outcomes. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90.125pt, 411.35pt, "LECO couples highly localized energy deposition with reverse-bias current localization ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 432.37pt, "and thermally activated interfacial evolution, thus, the processed contact state is determined ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 453.4pt, "by spatial-temporal fields rather than by a single tool setting. Consequently, purely empirical ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 473.67pt, "recipe tuning is sensitive to (i) variability in wafer-to-wafer and tool drift, and (ii) offers ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 494.68pt, "limited ability to extrapolate toward long term stability under combined electrical, thermal, ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 514.95pt, "and environmental stress. A predictive design framework therefore treats LECO as a coupled ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 535.97pt, "multiphysics problem in which process inputs are mapped to interfacial state variables and, in ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 557pt, "turn, to reliability outcomes, as summarized by the hierarchical workflow in Figure 9. The ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 577.25pt, "modeling hierarchy adopted here has three layers that mirror this workflow: (i) a transient ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 598.27pt, "finite element (FE) core that resolves the temperature field and current density during laser ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 618.55pt, "exposure under reverse bias, (ii) a metric extraction step that compresses these fields into an ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 639.55pt, "effective diffusion depth and a local areal energy density, and (iii) a calibration plus surrogate ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 660.58pt, "layer that propagates regime boundaries across recipe space to enable manufacturing-oriented ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 680.85pt, "process windows and digital-twin control. This hierarchy supports efficiency and durability ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 701.87pt, "co-optimization and advances sustainability by reducing rework, yield loss, and excess ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 722.13pt, "thermal budget while maintaining stable, low-resistance contact performance [130,131]. ")
]

