  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.1pt, 84.08pt, "conventional depth profiling for light elements, which motivates using complementary phase-")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 105.1pt, "sensitive methods when the key instabilities are chemistry-driven [142]. ")
  #line-at(90.125pt, 131.37pt, "A practical community target is a minimum characterization set for LECO contacts that ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 152.37pt, "reports (i) phase identity and continuity, (ii) barrier integrity metrics, and (iii) microcontact ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 172.65pt, "size and areal density statistics, then links these quantities to electrical regime descriptors and ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 193.67pt, "reliability classes. For Cu-containing stacks, depth profiling is additionally required to ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 214.7pt, "quantify metal migration pathways, and damp-heat studies already demonstrate that SIMS ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 234.95pt, "can detect Cu in the Si bulk after extended stress, which makes diffusion-aware interface ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 255.97pt, "descriptors essential for bankability [143]. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 15.775pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.1pt, 287.5pt, "8.3 Cu long-term reliability under LECO-relevant activation ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90.125pt, 316.03pt, "Cu-containing metallization is increasingly attractive for cost reasons, but it introduces ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 337.05pt, "durability risks dominated by diffusion, barrier compromise, and moisture-assisted corrosion. ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 357.33pt, "These mechanisms are sensitive to local temperature excursions and to current localization, ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 378.32pt, "and therefore they interact directly with LECO physics. Broad reviews of Cu-plated ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 399.35pt, "metallization emphasize reliability, adhesion, and contact integrity as principal barriers to ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 419.62pt, "adoption, with additional constraints arising from outdoor exposure requirements [6]. Earlier ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 440.62pt, "reviews of Ni/Cu plating likewise highlight the process complexity and the sensitivity of ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 460.9pt, "outcomes to interface preparation and barrier quality, which increases the importance of ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 481.92pt, "stability margins when additional activation steps are introduced [144]. ")
  #line-at(90.125pt, 508.95pt, "The critical evidence gap is long-duration testing of LECO-treated Cu stacks under ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 529.22pt, "combined stress profiles that reflect field operation, including temperature, humidity, ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 550.23pt, "electrical bias, and thermal cycling. Damp-heat studies of Cu-plated cells demonstrate ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 570.5pt, "junction-related degradation consistent with Cu migration, and they show that materials ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 591.52pt, "choices such as encapsulant can strongly influence whether Cu transport becomes ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 612.53pt, "performance-limiting [119]. Complementary work provides direct evidence of Cu out ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 632.8pt, "diffusion through capping layers during damp-heat exposure and detects elevated Cu levels at ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 653.83pt, "the Si surface and in the Si bulk, reinforcing the need to treat Cu transport as a bankability ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 674.1pt, "constraint rather than a secondary effect [143]. From a module-reliability perspective, ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 695.1pt, "electromigration and delamination risks become more consequential as current density ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 716.13pt, "increases and as metallization strategies diversify, which further motivates LECO ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 736.4pt, "qualification protocols that are incubation-sensitive and spatially resolved [107]. ")
]

