  #line-at(72.1pt, 87.08pt, "8.4 Fine-line metallization scaling and current localization ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90.125pt, 115.6pt, "Fine-line scaling reduces shading and metal consumption, but it increases local current ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 136.62pt, "density and narrows the tolerance to interfacial nonuniformity. As finger widths shrink and ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 156.9pt, "aspect ratios rise, a small fraction of weak or over-activated contacts can dominate resistance ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 177.9pt, "drift and introduce localized heating. Recent fine-line screen-printing work demonstrates 20 ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 198.92pt, "µm-class openings and quantifies the coupled impacts on grid geometry and electrical ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 219.2pt, "performance, which provides a concrete scaling backdrop for LECO regime transferability ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 240.2pt, "[145]. In this scaling limit, robustness margins must be defined in terms of current ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 260.47pt, "localization, not only in terms of mean contact resistivity, because geometry-driven current ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 281.5pt, "crowding can shift devices closer to the damage boundary even at unchanged nominal ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 302.53pt, "recipes. ")
  #line-at(90.125pt, 328.8pt, "For passivating-contact architectures, scaling also demands preservation of passivation ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 349.8pt, "quality and avoidance of metallization-induced recombination. Reviews of metallization for ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 370.08pt, "SiO")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.25pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90.875pt, 370.83pt, "x")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(95.375pt, 370.08pt, "/poly-Si passivating contacts emphasize that paste chemistry, thermal budgets, and ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 391.1pt, "contact formation pathways remain central to industrialization, which means that any ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 411.35pt, "additional local activation step must be evaluated against passivation retention constraints ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 432.37pt, "[146]. Interface chemistry further couples into this problem through hydrogen and defect ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 453.4pt, "dynamics at the tunnel oxide interface, where nanoscale characterization has shown that light ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 473.67pt, "elements and subtle compositional changes can be decisive for stability [142]. LECO-specific ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 494.68pt, "evidence on TOPCon stacks shows that passivation degradation can occur when the process ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 514.95pt, "is not properly bounded, reinforcing that fine-line scaling and passivation retention are ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 535.97pt, "inseparable from the regime-boundary logic in Section 7 [123]. ")
  #line-at(90.125pt, 563pt, "A priority research direction is therefore to establish scaling rules that connect finger ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 582.5pt, "geometry and microcontact statistics to allowable ranges of ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(360.45pt, 582.5pt, "𝐸")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 8.25pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(366.48pt, 585.53pt, "𝐴")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(373.23pt, 582.5pt, ", ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(379.23pt, 582.5pt, "𝑇")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 8.25pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(385.25pt, 585.53pt, "𝑚𝑎𝑥")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(404.02pt, 582.5pt, "nd current crowding ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 604.28pt, "descriptors such as ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(165.95pt, 604.28pt, "𝐶")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 8.25pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(171.98pt, 607.27pt, "𝐽")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(176.48pt, 604.28pt, ", then validate those rules against long-term drift and scatter. This shifts ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 626.8pt, "recipe selection from geometry-specific tuning to transferable design margins. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 15.775pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.1pt, 659.07pt, "8.5 AI-guided parameter optimization and digital twin ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 686.1pt, "deployment ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90.125pt, 714.63pt, "LECO is governed by a coupled, high-dimensional parameter space, laser power, scan ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 735.65pt, "strategy, spot size, overlap, and bias, as well as upstream firing history and metallization ")
  #line-at(72.1pt, 756.675pt, "state. One-factor tuning is inefficient in this setting and increases the likelihood of selecting ")
]

